# Docker Commands Reference

## Container Management

### Start/Stop Services
```bash
# Start all services
docker-compose up -d

# Stop all services
docker-compose down

# Restart specific service
docker-compose restart wordpress
docker-compose restart db
docker-compose restart mailcatcher

# View running containers
docker-compose ps

# View container logs
docker-compose logs -f wordpress
docker-compose logs --tail=50 db
```

### Container Access
```bash
# Access WordPress container shell
docker exec -it wp-pdev-wordpress bash

# Access MySQL container
docker exec -it wp-pdev-db mysql -uwordpress -pwordpress wordpress

# Access WP-CLI container
docker exec -it wp-pdev-cli bash
```

## WP-CLI Operations

### User Management
```bash
# Create admin user
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp user create testadmin admin@example.com --role=administrator --user_pass=password

# List users
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp user list

# Reset password
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp user update 1 --user_pass=newpassword
```

### Plugin Management
```bash
# List plugins
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp plugin list

# Activate/Deactivate
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp plugin activate choice-uft
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp plugin deactivate choice-uft

# Install plugin
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp plugin install plugin-slug --activate

# Update plugins
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp plugin update --all
```

### Database Operations
```bash
# Export database
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp db export - > backup.sql

# Import database
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp db import < backup.sql

# Search and replace
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp search-replace 'old-domain.com' 'localhost:8080'

# Optimize database
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp db optimize

# Reset database
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp db reset --yes
```

### Cache Management
```bash
# Clear object cache
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp cache flush

# Clear transients
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp transient delete --all

# Clear rewrite rules
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp rewrite flush
```

## File Operations

### Copy Files To/From Container
```bash
# Copy file to container
docker cp local-file.php wp-pdev-wordpress:/var/www/html/

# Copy file from container
docker cp wp-pdev-wordpress:/var/www/html/wp-config.php ./wp-config-backup.php

# Copy entire directory
docker cp ./my-plugin wp-pdev-wordpress:/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/
```

### File Permissions
```bash
# Fix WordPress permissions
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/html/wp-content
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress find /var/www/html/wp-content -type d -exec chmod 755 {} \;
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress find /var/www/html/wp-content -type f -exec chmod 644 {} \;

# Make uploads writable
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress chmod -R 777 /var/www/html/wp-content/uploads
```

## Debugging

### View Logs
```bash
# Apache error log
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress tail -f /var/log/apache2/error.log

# Apache access log
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress tail -f /var/log/apache2/access.log

# WordPress debug log
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress tail -f /var/www/html/wp-content/debug.log

# MySQL slow query log
docker exec wp-pdev-db tail -f /var/log/mysql/slow.log
```

### Monitor Resources
```bash
# Container stats
docker stats wp-pdev-wordpress wp-pdev-db

# Container processes
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress ps aux

# Disk usage
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress df -h
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress du -sh /var/www/html/*

# Memory usage
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress free -m
```

### Network Debugging
```bash
# Test connectivity between containers
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress ping -c 3 db
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress ping -c 3 mailcatcher

# Check listening ports
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress netstat -tuln

# Test database connection
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress mysql -hdb -uwordpress -pwordpress -e "SELECT 1"

# Test mail server
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress telnet mailcatcher 1025
```

## Development Workflows

### Quick Reset Environment
```bash
# Full reset (careful - deletes everything!)
docker-compose down -v
docker-compose up -d
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp core install \
  --url=http://localhost:8080 \
  --title="Dev Site" \
  --admin_user=admin \
  --admin_email=admin@example.com \
  --admin_password=password
```

### Sync with Production
```bash
# Export production database
ssh production "wp db export - | gzip" > prod-db.sql.gz

# Import to local
gunzip -c prod-db.sql.gz | docker exec -i wp-pdev-cli wp db import -

# Update URLs
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp search-replace 'https://production.com' 'http://localhost:8080'

# Sync uploads
rsync -avz production:/path/to/uploads/ ./wp-content/uploads/
```

### Create Test Content
```bash
# Generate test posts
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp post generate --count=10 --post_type=post

# Generate test pages
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp post generate --count=5 --post_type=page

# Create test users
for i in {1..5}; do
  docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp user create user$i user$i@example.com --role=subscriber
done
```

## Maintenance

### Clean Up
```bash
# Remove unused images
docker image prune -a

# Remove unused volumes
docker volume prune

# Remove stopped containers
docker container prune

# Full system cleanup
docker system prune -a --volumes

# Check disk usage
docker system df
```

### Backup & Restore
```bash
# Full backup
mkdir backup-$(date +%Y%m%d)
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp db export - > backup-$(date +%Y%m%d)/database.sql
tar -czf backup-$(date +%Y%m%d)/wp-content.tar.gz ./wp-content
cp docker-compose.yml backup-$(date +%Y%m%d)/
cp .env backup-$(date +%Y%m%d)/

# Restore from backup
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp db import < backup-20240101/database.sql
tar -xzf backup-20240101/wp-content.tar.gz
```

### Update Containers
```bash
# Pull latest images
docker-compose pull

# Recreate containers with new images
docker-compose up -d --force-recreate

# Build custom image (if using Dockerfile)
docker-compose build --no-cache
docker-compose up -d
```

## Troubleshooting

### Container Won't Start
```bash
# Check logs
docker-compose logs wordpress

# Check container status
docker ps -a

# Inspect container
docker inspect wp-pdev-wordpress

# Force recreate
docker-compose down
docker-compose up -d --force-recreate
```

### Permission Issues
```bash
# Reset ownership
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/html

# Check current permissions
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress ls -la /var/www/html/wp-content/
```

### Database Connection Issues
```bash
# Test connection
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress mysql -hdb -uroot -proot -e "SHOW DATABASES"

# Check environment variables
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress printenv | grep MYSQL

# Recreate database container
docker-compose down db
docker-compose up -d db
```

## Custom Scripts

### Health Check Script
```bash
#!/bin/bash
echo "Checking WordPress health..."
curl -f http://localhost:8080/wp-admin/install.php > /dev/null 2>&1
if [ $? -eq 0 ]; then
  echo "✅ WordPress is running"
else
  echo "❌ WordPress is not responding"
fi

echo "Checking database..."
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp db check > /dev/null 2>&1
if [ $? -eq 0 ]; then
  echo "✅ Database is healthy"
else
  echo "❌ Database issues detected"
fi

echo "Checking MailCatcher..."
curl -f http://localhost:1080 > /dev/null 2>&1
if [ $? -eq 0 ]; then
  echo "✅ MailCatcher is running"
else
  echo "❌ MailCatcher is not responding"
fi
```

### Quick Deploy Script
```bash
#!/bin/bash
# Deploy changes to container
echo "Deploying changes..."
docker cp ./wp-content/plugins/choice-uft wp-pdev-wordpress:/var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/
docker exec wp-pdev-wordpress chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/html/wp-content/plugins/choice-uft
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp plugin deactivate choice-uft
docker exec wp-pdev-cli wp plugin activate choice-uft
echo "✅ Deployment complete"
```

